# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER add `.standards/` or `bin/<script>` symlinks here — they are COMMITTED.
# lacta and best_year both ignored `.standards/` and `bin/release` after
# committing them: every file upstream added later was silently ignored on
# sync, and a fresh clone of best_year had no bin/release.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Environment — .env.example and .envrc are committed; everything else is local
# (catches .env, .env.prod, .env.local, .env.stage, foo.env).
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example

# PR review files
.pr-context.md
pr-review-*.md

# Task files (anchored — an un-anchored `tasks/` hid Elixir's lib/mix/tasks/ in lacta)
/tasks.json
/tasks/

# Claude Code local state: personal settings, runtime locks
# (scheduled_tasks.lock), in-session worktrees, hook logs (stop-test.sh keeps
# failing runs here)
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.lock
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/logs/

# Rendered design docs (just docs-pdf) — reproducible from docs/design/
publish/

# Mobile / Firebase credentials — harmless in projects without them.
# Commit stand-ins instead: google-services.json.template, Secrets.example.*
# Keep release keystores OUTSIDE the working tree; one ignore pattern is all
# that stands between an in-repo keystore and a `git add -A`.
*.jks
*.keystore
key.properties
keystore.properties
secrets.properties
serviceAccountKey.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
google-services.json
Secrets.swift
firebase-debug*.log
firestore-debug.log
ui-debug.log
.firebase/
